# THE TOOLCHAIN THIS REPOSITORY IS BUILT WITH. This is the only file that pins a
# version: `mise install` reads it, `.github/workflows/ci.yml` installs from it
# through `jdx/mise-action` and re-declares none of the four strings, and
# `bin/check-toolchain.sh` fails the build if a literal is ever copied back
# beside the manifest.
#
# The names are mise's. `tree-sitter` here is the CLI, which npm calls
# `tree-sitter-cli`; both publish the same version number.
#
# Required and deliberately unpinned: mise itself, python3, perl, shasum and
# tar. None of them decides what gets built (python3 copies sections of
# LANGUAGE.md verbatim; perl runs a five-token alarm; shasum and tar handle an
# archive this repository also created), so a version line would assert a
# requirement nobody has measured. `bin/check-toolchain.sh --env` checks each
# is present, and that the four below resolve to binaries mise owns — an
# unmanaged copy holding the pinned number passes every version comparison
# while the build runs on a toolchain nothing here installed.

erlang 28.5
rebar 3.27.0
node 24.19.0
tree-sitter 0.25.10
